# 17. Conclusion

The analysis of the supplied synthetic pharmacy sales dataset shows total sales of 1,165 units and total revenue of 54,260.

Generic products account for the majority of unit volume, while branded products account for the majority of revenue.

Vitamin D3 is the largest individual revenue contributor in the supplied transactions, followed by Atorvastatin and Azithromycin.

The analysis also demonstrates the importance of including cost, inventory and readable date fields in future versions of the dataset. These fields would allow complete margin, growth and inventory-priority analysis.

No unsupported cost, margin or growth figures have been assumed.

